WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.840
In this video, you clone a running virtual machine, disks included, to get an identical copy for testing or scaling out without rebuilding it.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:17.360
On the Virtual Machines page, open the action menu of the virtual machine you want to copy.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.810
Select Clone.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:26.610
Keep Clone volume data selected, so the copy gets its own disks with the same contents.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.830
Enter a name for the new virtual machine.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.820
Keep the run strategy, so the clone starts as soon as it is created.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.880
Select Create.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:49.340
SUSE Virtualization copies the disk and starts the clone. It now runs next to the original, with its own IP address.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:58.132
The clone is an independent virtual machine with its own disks. Next, you create a Windows virtual machine.
